        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Tweedia, Crossandra\n- Plant families: Apocynaceae, Acanthaceae\n- Places: Africa, Madagascar, Arabia, Indian subcontinent\n- Topics: plant taxonomy, flowering plants\n\nFacts:\n- Tweedia is a genus of flowering plants in the Apocynaceae family.\n- Tweedia was first described as a genus in 1835.\n- Crossandra is a genus of plants in the Acanthaceae family.\n- Crossandra comprises 54 species.\n- Crossandra occurs in Africa, Madagascar, Arabia, and the Indian subcontinent.\n- Crossandra is known as கனகாம்பரம் in Tamil and ಕನಕಾಂಬರ in Kannada.",
